--- a/docs/plat/ax630c.rst	1969-12-31 17:00:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/docs/plat/ax630c.rst	1969-12-31 17:00:00.000000000 -0700
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Axera AX630C
+============
+
+The Axera AX630C (AX620E family) is a dual Cortex-A53 SoC with a GIC-400,
+found on boards such as the Sipeed NanoKVM-Pro and MaixCAM2.
+
+This port provides BL31 only. The SoC boots from an on-chip ROM into a vendor
+first-stage loader, which trains DRAM, brings up the clock tree and the console
+UART, loads the boot images from flash and enters BL31 at EL3 with the MMU off.
+That loader passes an ordinary ``bl_params_t`` v2 chain in ``x0`` and the
+standard platform cookie in ``x3``, so no ``RESET_TO_BL31`` handling is needed.
+
+Platform summary
+----------------
+
+======================== =========================================
+CPUs                     2 x Cortex-A53, one cluster
+Interrupt controller     GIC-400 at ``0x01850000``
+Console                  UART0 (16550) at ``0x04880000``, 208 MHz
+Generic timer            24 MHz
+BL31 load address        ``0x40040000``, in a 256 KiB window
+BL32                     none
+BL33 entry               supplied by the loader
+======================== =========================================
+
+PSCI support
+------------
+
+``CPU_ON``, ``CPU_OFF`` and ``SYSTEM_RESET``.
+
+The SoC has no CPU power controller. Each core owns a pair of scratch
+registers in the system-global block that act as a release mailbox: a core that
+is not running waits on ``WFE``, reloads its pair on each wake, and branches to
+the 40-bit address it finds there once it is non-zero. The boot ROM leaves the
+secondary core in exactly that loop, so ``CPU_ON`` is a mailbox write and an
+``SEV``, and ``CPU_OFF`` re-enters the same loop from BL31.
+
+``SYSTEM_RESET`` arms watchdog 0 with a reload of zero. That is the only reset
+on this SoC that reaches the whole chip. There is no ``SYSTEM_OFF``: nothing
+inside the SoC can remove its own supply.
+
+Building
+--------
+
+.. code:: shell
+
+    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-none-elf- PLAT=ax630c bl31
+
+The resulting ``bl31.bin`` is loaded verbatim to ``0x40040000``. How it is
+wrapped for flash is a property of the loader on a given board, not of this
+port.
